# Bots understand affixes (m7, owner 2026-11-26): a bot in a real player's group scores an affixed item with its affix stats
# (mod_arpg hook in playerbots StatsWeightCalculator, // ARPG:). A blue (1489, 2-3 affixes) rolled for the bot: its score
# with the hook is higher than the template-only score.

> .arpg test setup Arpgtest 20 elwynn-northshire
? ok .*\(online\)
~ 4000
> .arpg test botscore Arpgtest any 1489
? ok botscore bot=\S+ item=1489 affixes=[23] affix_sum=[1-9]\d* \(ok\) with=\d+\.\d without=\d+\.\d gain=\d+\.\d equipped_affixed=[1-9]
# Joining the group rolled affixes on the bot's own equipped greens/blues (Arpg.Bots.PartyGear, one tier below).
# gain = with - without is never negative; it can be 0 when the rolled stats are ones the bot's spec does not value.
# Loot still on a corpse (Need rolls, m7 3b.3): a planned blue - the bot sees its affixes (middle of their ranges) before
# anyone loots it.
> .arpg test planscore Arpgtest any 1489
*20 ok planscore bot=\S+ item=1489 rp=-\d+ planned_sum=[1-9]\d* \(planned\)
> .arpg config set Arpg.Bots.AffixScoring 0
? ok
> .arpg test botscore Arpgtest any 1489
? affix_sum=0 \(off\)
> .arpg config set Arpg.Bots.AffixScoring 1
? ok
> .arpg test botscore Arpgtest any ungroup
? ok ungrouped
